### Complete Calculator Program Overview

```c
#include <stdio.h>

int main(void)
{
    int num1, num2; // Declare two integer variables

    // Prompt user for the first number and read it
    printf("Enter the first integer: ");
    scanf("%i", &num1);

    // Prompt user for the second integer and read it
    printf("Enter the second integer: ");
    scanf("%i", &num2);

    // Calculate and print the sum
    printf("Sum: %i\n", num1 + num2);

    // Calculate and print the difference
    printf("Difference: %i\n", num1 - num2);

    // Calculate and print the product
    printf("Product: %i\n", num1 * num2);

    // Calculate and print the floating-point quotient (remember type casting!)
    printf("Quotient (float): %.2f\n", (float)num1 / num2);

    return 0;
}
```

**Key Takeaways:**
- Variables store data.
- `scanf` reads user input (requires `&`).
- `printf` displays output (requires format specifiers).
- Arithmetic operators perform calculations.
- Type casting is vital for accurate floating-point division.

